{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791802302,"nonce":"E3eg4a6GehvsiZg1/ERdiqLI2Ds=","title":"CSS theme watcher is disposed with the first presentation owner","message":"Reproduced against local AshUI 4d154c8 while reviewing ChimpMonk's editor in dark and light. If the first Css.load runs inside Owner.root, disposing that root also disposes Css.theme's Watch. The static themeWatched flag and themeVariables cache survive, so the next ThemeState.init and a newly mounted tree retain the first theme's CSS variables.\n\nThe installed Restrained light Primary token is #0A6CF0, but TreeSnapshot reads the old dark CSS primary #4f94ff. This leaves a remounted workspace with mixed theme colours.\n\nFocused reproducer is in ChimpMonk at repro/ashui_theme_owner/Repro.hx. It loads #probe { color: var(--primary); } inside a dark Owner.root, disposes the owner and tree, installs Light, creates a second owner/tree, and compares the actual CSS colour with ThemeState.get().color(Primary).\n\nCompile from ChimpMonk:\nhaxe -cp repro/ashui_theme_owner -cp ../ashui/haxe -cp ../hlwindow/haxe -lib tink_hxx --macro 'ashui.ui.Markup.enable()' -main Repro -hl /tmp/chimpmonk-svg-icons/theme-owner.hl\n\nStage the existing AshUI blinc_abi native library beside the binary and run:\nash --preset application /tmp/chimpmonk-svg-icons/theme-owner.hl\n\nObserved:\ndark: #4f94ff\nlight CSS: #4f94ff; light token: #0A6CF0\nUncaught exception: CSS theme watch was disposed with the first presentation owner\n\nCss.theme() creates new Watch under the current presentation Owner. The global theme watcher should have application lifetime, or be recreated when its owner disappears. ChimpMonk initializes theme and CSS before entering the presentation owner; this keeps the current editor correct, but other callers should not need that ordering to avoid stale global CSS.\n\nAcceptance: the exact reproducer passes; CSS theme variables refresh after tree disposal/remount and scheme changes without retaining disposed owners or duplicate watchers.","files":null}]}